of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le18ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Jobs and Work"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A common topic for small talk in English is jobs and work. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: What do you do? <br>   <span class=\"strong\">Sam</span>: I work in advertising. My office is on Main Street. I really enjoy it. I can't complain! How about you?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can ask about someone's job using the question <span class=\"italic\">What do you do? </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is generally a \u2018safe' topic and one that many people like to talk about.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You usually give a brief description of the job, the location of the job and your opinion of it."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the First Conditional to talk about real possibilities in the future."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Gloria</span>: If he gets married, we'll never see him.<br><span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: I know!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will do   something. In that condition, something else will happen."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">If </span> clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Main Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If he gets married,\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" we will never see him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If they get married, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"he will have to get a better apartment.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shift "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a period of time you work at a job "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We have long shifts at work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about jobs and work."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "benefit "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a form of additional payment at work (vacation time, pension, health care)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: We have great benefits at work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to be engaged"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to promise to marry someone "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: John and Sandra are engaged."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to propose "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to ask someone to marry you "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: John proposed to Sandra."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to complain"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to express feelings of pain or unhappiness "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can't complain about my job- it is great."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le18ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine you have some good news."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write an e-mail to your friend telling them all about it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask your friend to read your e-mail out loud. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write an e-mail about some good news."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I send it to a friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "My friend reads the e-mail aloud and we talk about it."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le18ob10re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le18ob10re2img06.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le18ob10re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Oh, hey. It's an e-mail from John.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: What does it say?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Hi, Peter. How's life? Work is good on the cruise ship. We have long shifts, but great benefits. I can't complain! Life is getting interesting for me. I have some news for you. Sandra and I are engaged! That's right - we're getting married. Crazy, eh? I proposed yesterday and she said yes! I'll buy a ring next week. Call me later so we can talk about it. Say hi to Sal and V for me too. Talk to you soon, John.", "id": 1, "time": "2000", "image": "engenn5le18ob10re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: What? He's engaged? Wow!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I know! I can't believe it! If he gets married, we will never see him! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Well, we never see him anyway. He works on a cruise ship.", "id"